    "body": "> This has a build error, probably you need to add a `data-x-href` in the dependencies section.\r\n\r\nThanks — added\r\n\r\n> We've been recently adding attribute change steps to be more rigorous about when attributes change (#1571), but, I think demanding that for the `<link>` section is not necessary at this time.\r\n\r\n✅ OK\r\n\r\n> That section already has lots of vaguer \"when the `x` attribute is set\" language. See also [#8138 (comment)](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/8138#issuecomment-1198819101).\r\n\r\nYeah I guess it adds some difficulty for implementors — including difficulty for implementors to provide reviewers with spec references for implementation-change patches. I wonder how much of this has so far gotten implemented in a particular UA just based on an implementor saying _“This is what UA X and UA Y already do, so we need to do it too, for interop”_ (and UA X and/or Y having implemented based just on assumptions rather than clear requirements…)\r\n\r\n",
